{"id": "tea:pancapadika-vivarana:bhava", "source": "src:pancapadika-vivarana", "location": {"ref": "bhava"}, "paraphrase": "Ignorance is a positive (bhāva-rūpa) entity, though indescribable, known through perception ('I am ignorant', 'I did not know anything' on waking from sleep), inference and presumption; it is removed by knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:bhavarupa-avidya"], "concepts": ["cpt:bhavarupa-avidya"], "disputes": ["dsp:bhavarupa-avidya"], "notes": "Topic-level reference.", "teachers": ["tch:prakasatman"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancapadika-vivarana:locus", "source": "src:pancapadika-vivarana", "location": {"ref": "locus"}, "paraphrase": "Ignorance has pure consciousness (Brahman) as both its locus and its object; the insentient cannot be the locus of ignorance and the jīva is itself a product of ignorance.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:avidya"], "concepts": ["cpt:avidya"], "disputes": ["dsp:locus-of-avidya"], "notes": "Topic-level reference.", "teachers": ["tch:prakasatman"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancapadika-vivarana:reflection", "source": "src:pancapadika-vivarana", "location": {"ref": "reflection"}, "paraphrase": "The reflection (the jīva) is real and identical with the prototype (bimba), as the face in the mirror is the face itself; only the adjunct makes it appear different. Īśvara is the prototype consciousness.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:pratibimba", "trm:bimba"], "concepts": ["cpt:pratibimba-vada"], "disputes": ["dsp:how-the-one-appears-as-many"], "notes": "Topic-level reference.", "teachers": ["tch:prakasatman"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancapadika-vivarana:sravana", "source": "src:pancapadika-vivarana", "location": {"ref": "sravana"}, "paraphrase": "Hearing (śravaṇa) — the ascertainment of the Upaniṣads' purport — is the principal means, enjoined by a restrictive injunction (niyama-vidhi); reflection and contemplation are its auxiliaries; the sentence itself produces immediate knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:sravana"], "practices": ["prc:sravana"], "disputes": ["dsp:sravana-alone-liberates"], "notes": "Topic-level reference.", "teachers": ["tch:prakasatman"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
